## 14.6 Accounting Integration

Every posted transaction must generate appropriate accounting entries.

Examples:

- Sales invoice: Debit customer/cash and credit sales/tax accounts.
- Purchase invoice: Debit inventory and applicable input tax accounts, credit supplier/company payable.
- Customer receipt: Debit cash/bank and credit customer receivable.
- Supplier payment: Debit payable and credit cash/bank.
- Sales return: Reverse the relevant revenue, tax, receivable, and inventory/COGS effects.
- Expense voucher: Debit expense and credit cash/bank/payable.

Use configurable tax and accounting rules.

Support transaction reversals through controlled reversal entries rather than silently editing posted accounting records.

